{"type":"record","name":"StrikeInvasionWallRow","namespace":"com.optionsedge.contracts.strikeinvasion","doc":"The shadow-wall cache entry of one strike: the resting CALL ask size of the newest accepted heatmap frame, stamped with the frame generation that wrote it. Held only in the service's in-memory, non-logged wall store. Internal evidence record of strike-invasion-service: it crosses a Kafka repartition topic (and, per strike, a state-store changelog) declared by that service, never a public contract. PRICE DOMAIN: every decimal(38,18) field accepts exactly the finite doubles whose shortest round-trip text has at most 18 fractional digits and magnitude below 1e20, and never negative zero; any other value is refused by the codec (never rounded) and the service counts and logs the refusal instead of publishing.","fields":[{"name":"strike","type":{"type":"bytes","logicalType":"decimal","precision":38,"scale":18}},{"name":"callAskSize","type":"long"},{"name":"generation","type":"long"},{"name":"asOfEventTimeMs","type":"long"}]}